A Class Diagram is a UML structural diagram that represents the classes in a system, their attributes, methods, and relationships with other classes.

What does it show in Lord of Realms?

It represents the internal structure of the game.
- Game: Controls the overall game flow.
- GameWindow: Manages the graphical user interface using Java Swing.
- StoryManager: Handles story progression and scene loading.
- StoryScene: Stores individual story scene information.
- Player: Manages player statistics such as HP, Qi, EXP, and gold.
- Inventory: Manages collected items.
- Item: Represents individual items and their properties.
- CombatManager: Handles combat operations and damage calculation.
Purpose: To understand the structure of the application and relationships between different classes
